{
  "title": "📝 Word Problems — From Real Life to Equations",
  "hook": "A father is 30 years older than his son. In 5 years, his age will be three times his son's age. How old are they now? Problems like these appear everywhere — from planning finances to mixing chemicals. The trick is translating words into equations!",
  "explanation": "<p><b>Strategy for word problems:</b></p><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#7B1FA2;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Read and identify unknowns</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Assign variables: let x = ..., y = ...</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#7B1FA2;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Translate conditions into equations</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Each condition gives one equation</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#7B1FA2;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Solve the system</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Use substitution, elimination, or cross-multiplication</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#7B1FA2;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div><div><strong>Verify and interpret</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Check answer makes sense; reject negative ages, etc.</span></div></div></div><br><b>Common Types:</b><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:12px 0;font-size:0.88rem\"><tr><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Problem Type</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Example Setup</th><th style=\"background:#E3F2FD;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #BBDEFB;text-align:left;font-weight:700\">Key Relationship</th></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Age problems</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Father-son ages</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Present + years = future</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Speed-distance</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Boat in river</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Downstream speed = boat + current</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Number problems</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Two-digit number</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Number = 10(tens) + units</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Fraction problems</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Numerator/Denominator</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">If 2 added to num, fraction = ...</td></tr><tr><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Cost/quantity</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Pens and pencils</td><td style=\"padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid #E0E0E0\">Total cost = unit price × quantity</td></tr></table><div style=\"background:#FFF8E1;border-left:4px solid #FFB300;border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin:10px 0;font-size:0.88rem\">💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> Always double-check by substituting back into the original WORDS, not just the equations!</div>",
  "worked_example": "<b>Example:</b> A fraction becomes 4/5 if 1 is added to both numerator and denominator. If 5 is subtracted from both, it becomes 1/2. Find the fraction.<br><br><div style=\"margin:12px 0\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">1</div><div><strong>Let numerator = x, denominator = y</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">The fraction is x/y</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">2</div><div><strong>Condition 1: (x+1)/(y+1) = 4/5</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Cross-multiply: 5(x+1) = 4(y+1) → 5x − 4y = −1 … (1)</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">3</div><div><strong>Condition 2: (x−5)/(y−5) = 1/2</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Cross-multiply: 2(x−5) = 1(y−5) → 2x − y = 5 … (2)</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">4</div><div><strong>Solve: from (2), y = 2x − 5</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">Sub in (1): 5x − 4(2x−5) = −1 → 5x − 8x + 20 = −1 → −3x = −21 → x = 7</span></div></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:12px;margin-bottom:10px;align-items:flex-start\"><div style=\"min-width:32px;height:32px;border-radius:50%;background:#4A90D9;color:white;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:0.85rem\">5</div><div><strong>Find y</strong><br><span style=\"color:#555;font-size:0.88rem\">y = 2(7) − 5 = 9</span></div></div></div><div style=\"background:linear-gradient(135deg,#E3F2FD,#BBDEFB);border-left:4px solid #1565C0;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 16px;margin:12px 0;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:1.05rem;text-align:center\"><strong>The fraction is 7/9</strong></div><p>Verify: (7+1)/(9+1) = 8/10 = 4/5 ✓. (7−5)/(9−5) = 2/4 = 1/2 ✓.</p>",
